  "answer_text": "Here is a complete overview of the MLA and MP seats in Telangana:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MLA Seats (State Legislature)\n\n### Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)\n- There are **119 MLAs** in the Telangana Legislative Assembly, elected by the people. The state is divided into **119 constituencies** with roughly equal populations.\n\n### Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)\n- Elections take place to elect **40 members** to the Legislative Council, of whom 14 are elected by members of the Telangana Legislative Assembly, 14 by local authorities of the state, 6 are nominated by the Governor, 3 are elected by teachers, and 3 are elected by graduates of the state.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f MP Seats (Parliament)\n\n### Lok Sabha (Lower House)\n- Telangana has **17 Lok Sabha constituencies**, with 3 reserved for Scheduled Castes (SC) and 2 for Scheduled Tribes (ST).\n\n### Rajya Sabha (Upper House)\n- Telangana has **7 Rajya Sabha seats**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Summary Table\n\n| House | Type | Total Seats |\n|---|---|---|\n| Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) | State | 119 |\n| Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad) | State | 40 |\n| Lok Sabha | Parliament | 17 |\n| Rajya Sabha | Parliament | 7 |\n\n**Total MP seats = 24** (17 Lok Sabha + 7 Rajya Sabha)\n**Total MLA seats = 159** (119 Assembly + 40 Council)",
